/* Hinglish for the on-ramp chapter, the recovery panels and the pacing.

   Generated alongside the English source: the key is the English line exactly
   as it appears in the course, so a line that is later edited in English falls
   back to English rather than showing a translation of something else. */
Object.assign(window.HING = window.HING || {}, {
  'Which shape is this problem?':
    'Yeh samasya kis shape ki hai?',
  'Five shapes cover almost everything anyone asks an AI to do — and picking the right one decides how measurable the result can ever be.':
    'Paanch shapes lagbhag har us cheez ko cover kar leti hain jo koi AI se karwata hai — aur sahi shape chunna tay karta hai ki nateeja kabhi kitna naapa ja sakega.',
  'Name which of the five shapes a request actually is, before designing anything.':
    'Kuchh bhi design karne se pehle yeh naam lena ki koi request asal me paanch me se kaunsi shape hai.',
  'Say why two of the shapes can be graded automatically and three cannot.':
    'Yeh batana ki paanch me se do shapes machine se kyun jaanchi ja sakti hain aur teen nahi.',
  'Turn a vague ask from a colleague into the narrowest shape that still solves their problem.':
    'Kisi saathi ki dhundhli si maang ko us sabse sankri shape me badalna jo phir bhi unki samasya hal karti ho.',
  'The shape map for one real request':
    'Ek asli request ka shape map',
  'Take the vaguest AI request anyone has actually made of you and turn it into something buildable — which is mostly a matter of naming shapes and putting them in order.':
    'Sabse dhundhli AI request lijiye jo kisi ne sach me aapse ki ho aur use banane laayak cheez me badliye — jo zyadatar shapes ko naam dene aur unhe kram me lagane ka kaam hai.',
  'Write the request down in the exact words it was asked in. Do not tidy it.':
    'Request ko un hi shabdon me likhiye jinme woh maangi gayi thi. Use sudhaariye mat.',
  'Name what the person actually wants to happen differently on a Tuesday. One sentence.':
    'Likhiye ki woh insaan sach me chahta kya hai ki mangalwaar ko alag ho. Ek vaakya.',
  'Break it into steps, each with exactly one shape, in the order they must run.':
    'Use steps me todiye, har step me theek ek shape, us kram me jis kram me unhe chalna hai.',
  'Mark which steps have a right answer and which do not. Those are your measurable and unmeasurable halves.':
    'Nishaan lagaiye ki kaunse steps ka sahi jawaab hota hai aur kaunse ka nahi. Wahi aapke naapne laayak aur na-naapne laayak hisse hain.',
  'For each measurable step, say where an answer key would come from — who already makes that judgement today, and on what.':
    'Har naapne laayak step ke liye bataiye ki answer key kahan se aayegi — aaj yeh faisla kaun karta hai, aur kis aadhaar par.',
  'Write the one-paragraph reply you would send the person, describing what you would build first and why it is the smallest useful thing.':
    'Ek paragraph ka jawaab likhiye jo aap us insaan ko bhejenge, jisme ho ki aap sabse pehle kya banayenge aur wahi sabse chhoti kaam ki cheez kyun hai.',
  'Every step in your breakdown has exactly one shape.':
    'Aapke breakdown ke har step me theek ek shape hai.',
  'You can point at the steps that can be graded without a human reading the output.':
    'Aap un steps par ungli rakh sakte hain jinhe bina kisi insaan ke output padhe jaancha ja sakta hai.',
  'The thing you propose building first is measurable, and you can say what you would measure it against.':
    'Jo cheez aap pehle banane ka prastav de rahe hain woh naapi ja sakti hai, aur aap bata sakte hain ki use kiske against naapenge.',
  'A prompt is a specification':
    'Prompt ek specification hai',
  'Four moves that shape what comes back.':
    'Chaar moves jo tay karte hain ki kya waapas aayega.',
  'A test set, and one change at a time':
    'Ek test set, aur ek baar me ek badlaav',
  'How you tell better from different.':
    'Behtar aur alag me farq karne ka tareeka.',
  'No new setup. Bring the test set you built in Chapter 2.2 — you will use it once more, and then see why its rows were easy to grade for a reason you had not noticed.':
    'Koi naya setup nahi. Chapter 2.2 me banaya test set le aaiye — use ek baar aur istemaal karenge, aur phir dekhenge ki uski rows jaanchne me aasaan kyun thin, aur wajah woh nahi thi jo aapne socha tha.',
  'People bring you requests in the language of outcomes. <em>Can the AI handle our inbox. Can it help with contracts. Can it make the team faster.</em> None of those is a task. Underneath almost every one of them is one of five shapes, and which shape it is decides more than which model you pick.':
    'Log aapke paas requests nateejon ki bhasha me laate hain. <em>Kya AI hamara inbox sambhaal lega. Kya woh contracts me madad karega. Kya woh team ko tez kar dega.</em> Inme se koi task nahi hai. Inme se lagbhag har ek ke neeche paanch me se koi ek shape hoti hai, aur woh kaunsi shape hai yeh is se zyada tay karta hai ki aap kaunsa model chunte hain.',
  'Choosing the shape is the first design decision, it is made in a sentence, and it is the one most often skipped.':
    'Shape chunna pehla design faisla hai, ek vaakya me ho jaata hai, aur sabse zyada yahi chhoda jaata hai.',
  'shape':
    'shape',
  'the job':
    'kaam',
  'can a machine grade it?':
    'kya machine ise jaanch sakti hai?',
  '<strong>Classify</strong>':
    '<strong>Classify</strong>',
  'put this into one of these buckets':
    'ise inme se kisi ek bucket me daaliye',
  'Yes — there is a right answer':
    'Haan — ek sahi jawaab hota hai',
  '<strong>Extract</strong>':
    '<strong>Extract</strong>',
  'pull these specific fields out':
    'yeh khaas fields nikaal laaiye',
  'Yes — the value is in the document or it is not':
    'Haan — value document me hai ya nahi hai',
  '<strong>Summarise</strong>':
    '<strong>Summarise</strong>',
  'make this shorter without losing what matters':
    'ise chhota kijiye bina us cheez ko khoye jo maayne rakhti hai',
  'No — depends who is reading':
    'Nahi — yeh is par tika hai ki padh kaun raha hai',
  '<strong>Rewrite</strong>':
    '<strong>Rewrite</strong>',
  'same meaning, different form or tone':
    'wahi matlab, alag roop ya lehja',
  'No — but you can check what must not change':
    'Nahi — lekin aap jaanch sakte hain ki kya nahi badalna chahiye',
  '<strong>Generate</strong>':
    '<strong>Generate</strong>',
  'produce something that was not there':
    'aisi cheez banaiye jo thi hi nahi',
  'No — and this is where most projects start':
    'Nahi — aur zyadatar projects yahin se shuru hote hain',
  'The first two have right answers. That is not a small property — it is the difference between a feature you can measure on Monday and one you argue about for a quarter.':
    'Pehli do ke sahi jawaab hote hain. Yeh koi chhoti baat nahi — yahi farq hai us feature me jise aap somwaar ko naap sakte hain aur us me jis par aap ek quarter behes karte hain.',
  'Sort real requests into the five':
    'Asli requests ko paanchon me baantiye',
  'Write down six things people at your work have actually asked for from AI. Real requests, in their words, including the vague ones. Then put each into one of the five shapes.':
    'Chhah cheezein likhiye jo aapke kaam par logon ne sach me AI se maangi hain. Asli requests, unke shabdon me, dhundhli waali bhi. Phir har ek ko paanch shapes me se kisi ek me daaliye.',
  'Two things usually happen. Several requests turn out to be the same shape wearing different words. And at least one refuses to sit in any single box — which means it is not one task, it is two or three stapled together.':
    'Do cheezein aam taur par hoti hain. Kai requests nikal kar ek hi shape hoti hain, bas alag shabdon me. Aur kam se kam ek kisi bhi ek box me baithne se mana kar deti hai — jiska matlab hai ki woh ek task nahi hai, do-teen task ek saath jude hue hain.',
  'A request that will not fit one shape is not a hard problem. It is an unsplit problem.':
    'Jo request ek shape me nahi baithti woh mushkil samasya nahi hai. Woh bina bantee hui samasya hai.',
  'That last point is the whole value of this chapter. "Handle the inbox" is not a task. Underneath it is usually: <em>classify</em> the message by type, <em>extract</em> the account number, and <em>generate</em> a draft reply. Three shapes, three different difficulties, three different ways of failing — and only the first two can be measured without a human reading the output.':
    'Aakhri baat hi is chapter ki poori keemat hai. “Inbox sambhaalo” koi task nahi hai. Uske neeche aam taur par yeh hota hai: message ko type se <em>classify</em> kijiye, account number <em>extract</em> kijiye, aur ek draft reply <em>generate</em> kijiye. Teen shapes, teen alag mushkilein, fail hone ke teen alag tareeke — aur inme se sirf pehli do ko bina kisi insaan ke output padhe naapa ja sakta hai.',
  'Split the one that would not fit':
    'Jo nahi baithi thi use todiye',
  'Take the request that refused to sit in a box and break it into steps that each have exactly one shape. Write them in the order they would have to happen.':
    'Woh request lijiye jo kisi box me nahi baithi aur use aise steps me todiye jinme har ek ki theek ek shape ho. Unhe us kram me likhiye jis kram me unhe hona hoga.',
  'Three or four steps, and a surprise: usually only the last one is the hard, unmeasurable part. The rest are classification and extraction, which are cheap and checkable — and if the first steps are reliable, the last one has a much easier job.':
    'Teen-chaar steps, aur ek hairaani: aam taur par sirf aakhri waala hissa mushkil aur na-naapne laayak hota hai. Baaki classification aur extraction hain, jo saste aur jaanchne laayak hain — aur agar shuru ke steps bharosemand hain, to aakhri waale ka kaam kaafi aasaan ho jaata hai.',
  'This is also where the cost falls. A classification step can run on a small cheap model. Only the last step needs an expensive one, and only for the cases that reach it.':
    'Kharch bhi yahin girta hai. Classification ka step kisi chhote saste model par chal sakta hai. Sirf aakhri step ko mehnga model chahiye, aur woh bhi sirf un cases ke liye jo wahan tak pahunchte hain.',
  'Which shape, and what changes':
    'Kaunsi shape, aur kya badalta hai',
  'A colleague asks for "an AI that reviews contracts and flags risky clauses." Which shape is that, really?':
    'Ek saathi maangta hai “aisa AI jo contracts review kare aur khatre waale clauses par nishaan lagaye.” Yeh asal me kaunsi shape hai?',
  'Mostly classify, with extract underneath it. Each clause gets a bucket — standard, unusual, missing — and the risky ones need their text pulled out to show. Almost none of it is generation.':
    'Zyadatar classify, jiske neeche extract hai. Har clause ko ek bucket milta hai — aam, ajeeb, gayab — aur khatre waalon ka text dikhane ke liye nikaalna padta hai. Isme generation lagbhag hai hi nahi.',
  'Which changes everything about how you would build it. Classification has right answers, so you can build an answer key from a hundred clauses a lawyer has already judged, and know your quality before shipping. Had you taken "reviews contracts" at face value and built a generator, there would be nothing to measure and no way to defend it.':
    'Jisse yeh poora badal jaata hai ki aap ise banate kaise. Classification ke sahi jawaab hote hain, isliye aap sau aise clauses se answer key bana sakte hain jinhe koi vakeel pehle hi jaanch chuka hai, aur ship karne se pehle apni quality jaan sakte hain. Agar aap “contracts review” ko waisa hi maan kar ek generator bana dete, to naapne ko kuchh hota hi nahi aur defend karne ka koi tareeka nahi hota.',
  'Ask "which shape?" before "which model?" — and if the answer is more than one shape, you have found the design, not a complication.':
    '“Kaunsi shape?” “Kaunsa model?” se pehle poochhiye — aur agar jawaab ek se zyada shape hai, to aapne design dhoondh liya hai, koi uljhan nahi.',
  'Two of these shapes are worth a chapter each, because they are the two you will meet most and the two where a small amount of care produces a large amount of reliability. The next chapter takes the one with a right answer.':
    'In shapes me se do ek-ek chapter ki haqdaar hain, kyunki yahi do aapko sabse zyada milengi aur inhi do me thodi si mehnat bahut zyada bharosa deti hai. Agla chapter woh leta hai jiska sahi jawaab hota hai.',
  'Classification, the cheap reliable one':
    'Classification, sasti aur bharosemand waali',
  'The shape with a right answer — which makes it the only one you can improve on purpose rather than by feel.':
    'Woh shape jiska sahi jawaab hota hai — jisse yeh ekmatra aisi hai jise aap ehsaas ke bajaay soch-samajh kar behtar kar sakte hain.',
  'Build a classifier for a real category set and measure it honestly.':
    'Kisi asli category set ke liye classifier banana aur use imaandaari se naapna.',
  'Say which class your system is worst at, and what that costs the business.':
    'Yeh batana ki aapka system kis class par sabse kharaab hai, aur uska business par kya kharch hai.',
  'Explain why an overall accuracy figure usually hides the failure that matters.':
    'Yeh samjhana ki kul accuracy ka aankda aksar wahi failure kyun chhupa leta hai jo maayne rakhti hai.',
  'A classifier you would let route real work':
    'Aisa classifier jise aap asli kaam bhejne dein',
  'Build a classifier for a real category set at your work, measure it per class, and decide — with numbers — whether it is good enough to act on rather than merely to suggest.':
    'Apne kaam ke kisi asli category set ke liye classifier banaiye, use har class par naapiye, aur numbers ke saath tay kijiye ki woh sirf sujhaav dene ke bajaay kaam karne laayak hai ya nahi.',
  'Fix the categories. Include an <em>other</em> or <em>unclear</em> bucket; a set with no escape hatch forces wrong answers.':
    'Categories tay kijiye. Ek <em>other</em> ya <em>unclear</em> bucket rakhiye; bina nikaas waala set galat jawaab dene par majboor karta hai.',
  'Collect fifty real examples and label them yourself, before running anything.':
    'Pachaas asli examples jama kijiye aur kuchh bhi chalane se pehle unhe khud label kijiye.',
  'Build the classifier with two worked examples, one of which is a boundary case.':
    'Classifier ko do worked examples ke saath banaiye, jinme ek boundary case ho.',
  'Measure per class, not overall. Write the table.':
    'Har class par naapiye, kul par nahi. Table likhiye.',
  'For your worst class, write what each direction of error costs, and adjust the instruction so the boundary falls the cheaper way. Re-measure.':
    'Apni sabse kharaab class ke liye likhiye ki har disha ki galti ka kya kharch hai, aur instruction aise badliye ki boundary sasti disha me gire. Dobara naapiye.',
  'Decide the threshold: above what per-class number would you let this route work automatically, and below what would it only ever suggest?':
    'Threshold tay kijiye: har class ke kis number ke upar aap ise apne aap kaam bhejne denge, aur kis ke neeche yeh sirf sujhaav dega?',
  'You have per-class numbers from fifty examples you labelled before testing.':
    'Aapke paas un pachaas examples se har class ke numbers hain jinhe aapne test se pehle khud label kiya.',
  'You made one deliberate change to which way a boundary case falls, and measured the effect.':
    'Aapne jaan-boojh kar ek badlaav kiya ki boundary case kis taraf gire, aur uska asar naapa.',
  'You can state the number at which you would let it act unsupervised — and you are not currently above it, or you are and can say so.':
    'Aap woh number bata sakte hain jis par aap ise bina nigraani ke chalne denge — aur aap abhi uske upar nahi hain, ya hain aur yeh keh sakte hain.',
  'Five shapes, and which have right answers':
    'Paanch shapes, aur kinke sahi jawaab hote hain',
  'Classification is the one that can be graded.':
    'Classification wahi hai jise jaancha ja sakta hai.',
  'A test set is how you tell better from different':
    'Test set hi behtar aur alag me farq batata hai',
  'Here it becomes an answer key with real numbers.':
    'Yahan woh asli numbers waali answer key ban jaata hai.',
  'You will run one classifier many times.':
    'Aaj aap ek classifier kai baar chalayenge.',
  'Open <code>chapter-2-4</code>, run the warm-up cells, and bring twenty real examples of something at your work that gets sorted into categories — tickets by type, documents by department, requests by urgency.':
    '<code>chapter-2-4</code> kholiye, warm-up cells chalaiye, aur apne kaam ki kisi aisi cheez ke bees asli examples le aaiye jinhe categories me baanta jaata hai — tickets type se, documents department se, requests urgency se.',
  'Re-read your own test set with new eyes':
    'Apne hi test set ko nayi nazar se padhiye',
  'Open the ten-row test set from Chapter 2.2 and look at what you wrote in the "good answer contains" column.':
    'Chapter 2.2 ka das row ka test set kholiye aur dekhiye ki aapne “achchhe jawaab me kya hona chahiye” waale column me kya likha tha.',
  'If your task was classification or extraction, those rows are crisp — a value, a bucket, a yes. If it was summarisation, they are woolly, and grading them took judgement. That difference was never about your writing. It was the shape.':
    'Agar aapka kaam classification ya extraction tha, to woh rows saaf hain — ek value, ek bucket, ek haan. Agar summarisation tha, to woh dhundhli hain aur unhe jaanchne me raay lagi. Yeh farq kabhi aapke likhne ka nahi tha. Yeh shape ka tha.',
  'Classification is putting a thing into one of a fixed set of buckets. It is unglamorous, it is most of what useful software does, and it has the property no other shape has: somebody can say whether the answer was right.':
    'Classification matlab kisi cheez ko tay buckets me se ek me daalna. Yeh chamak-dhamak wali nahi hai, kaam ke zyadatar software yahi karte hain, aur isme woh khoobi hai jo kisi aur shape me nahi: koi bata sakta hai ki jawaab sahi tha ya nahi.',
  'A right answer means you can count. Counting means you can improve on purpose instead of by feel — which is the entire difference between engineering and hoping.':
    'Sahi jawaab hone ka matlab hai ki aap gin sakte hain. Ginti ka matlab hai ki aap ehsaas ke bajaay soch-samajh kar behtar kar sakte hain — aur engineering aur ummeed me poora farq yahi hai.',
  'Build one, badly, on purpose':
    'Ek banaiye, jaan-boojh kar kharaab',
  'Write the simplest possible version: the categories, one line of instruction, no examples.':
    'Sabse saral version likhiye: categories, ek line ka instruction, koi example nahi.',
  'Mostly right, and two kinds of wrong. Some genuinely misread. But some come back as <code>Billing.</code> or <code>the category is billing</code> — not a wrong answer, an unusable one. You asked for a label and got a sentence.':
    'Zyadatar sahi, aur do tarah ke galat. Kuchh sach me galat padhte hain. Lekin kuchh <code>Billing.</code> ya <code>the category is billing</code> ban kar aate hain — galat jawaab nahi, bekaar jawaab. Aapne label maanga tha aur vaakya mila.',
  'Fix the format problem with the move you already know — show it, do not describe it. Two worked examples, one of them an awkward case, and the shape stops drifting. Chapter 8 will remove the possibility entirely rather than discouraging it, but two examples get you most of the way today.':
    'Format ki samasya usi move se theek kijiye jo aap pehle se jaante hain — dikhaiye, bataiye mat. Do worked examples, jinme ek tedha ho, aur shape bhatakna band kar deti hai. Chapter 8 is sambhaavna ko hatotsahit karne ke bajaay poori tarah khatm kar dega, lekin aaj do examples aapko zyadatar raasta paar karwa dete hain.',
  'Now count properly':
    'Ab dhang se giniye',
  'Grade all twenty against what you know the answer to be, and count per class rather than overall.':
    'Bees ko us jawaab ke against jaanchiye jo aap jaante hain, aur kul ke bajaay har class par giniye.',
  'An overall figure that looks respectable — and one class that is far worse than the rest. It is almost always the rare one, or the one whose boundary with its neighbour is genuinely blurry.':
    'Ek kul aankda jo theek-thaak dikhta hai — aur ek class jo baaki se kahin kharaab hai. Woh lagbhag hamesha wahi hoti hai jo virle aati hai, ya jiski apne padosi se seema sach me dhundhli hai.',
  'The overall number is the one that gets quoted and the per-class numbers are the ones that matter. A system that is 92 per cent right overall and 40 per cent right on the urgent category is not a 92 per cent system.':
    'Kul number wahi hai jo quote hota hai aur har class ke numbers wahi hain jo maayne rakhte hain. Jo system kul milakar 92 pratishat sahi hai aur urgent category par 40 pratishat, woh 92 pratishat waala system nahi hai.',
  'Take your worst class. Write what actually happens to a real person when a message of that class is sent to the wrong bucket — and what happens in the reverse direction, when something else is wrongly sent to it.':
    'Apni sabse kharaab class lijiye. Likhiye ki jab us class ka message galat bucket me chala jaata hai to kisi asli insaan ke saath sach me kya hota hai — aur ulti disha me kya hota hai, jab koi aur cheez galti se usme daal di jaati hai.',
  'When a … is missed, … . When something is wrongly marked …, … .':
    'Jab koi … chhoot jaata hai, … . Jab kisi cheez par galti se … ka nishaan lagta hai, … .',
  'The two directions almost never cost the same. Missing an urgent complaint and wrongly flagging a routine one as urgent are both errors, and one of them is cheap. Once you can say which, you can deliberately make the system lean the cheap way — by making the boundary case fall into the safer bucket. That is a product decision, made with numbers, and it belongs to you rather than to whoever wrote the prompt.':
    'Dono dishaon ka kharch lagbhag kabhi ek jaisa nahi hota. Ek urgent shikayat chhoot jaana aur ek aam cheez par galti se urgent ka nishaan lag jaana, dono galtiyaan hain, aur inme se ek sasti hai. Jaise hi aap bata sakte hain ki kaunsi, aap system ko jaan-boojh kar sasti disha me jhuka sakte hain — boundary case ko surakshit bucket me giraa kar. Yeh ek product faisla hai, numbers ke saath liya gaya, aur yeh aapka hai, us insaan ka nahi jisne prompt likha.',
  'Notice how little of this was about AI. An answer key, per-class counts, and a judgement about which error is cheaper — the same instrument you would use to evaluate a hiring process or a triage desk.':
    'Dhyaan dijiye ki isme AI kitna kam tha. Ek answer key, har class ki ginti, aur yeh raay ki kaunsi galti sasti hai — wahi instrument jise aap hiring process ya triage desk jaanchne ke liye istemaal karte.',
  'The next shape has no right answer at all, which is why almost everybody who builds it ships it without knowing whether it works.':
    'Agli shape ka to koi sahi jawaab hi nahi hota, aur isiliye use banane waale lagbhag sab log use bina yeh jaane ship kar dete hain ki woh kaam karti bhi hai ya nahi.',
  'Summarising without losing the point':
    'Summarise karna, bina asli baat khoye',
  'The most requested feature, and the one whose failure is hardest to see — because a summary that lost the crucial line still reads beautifully.':
    'Sabse zyada maanga jaane waala feature, aur wahi jiski failure sabse mushkil se dikhti hai — kyunki jis summary se zaroori line chhoot gayi woh bhi khoobsurat hi padhi jaati hai.',
  'Say what a summary is for before writing the prompt that makes one.':
    'Summary banane waala prompt likhne se pehle yeh batana ki summary kis kaam ke liye hai.',
  'Test a summariser for the failure that matters — the thing it left out.':
    'Summariser ko us failure ke liye jaanchna jo maayne rakhti hai — us cheez ke liye jo woh chhod gaya.',
  'Explain why "it reads well" is the least useful thing you can say about a summary.':
    'Yeh samjhana ki “yeh achchha padha jaata hai” kisi summary ke baare me sabse bekaar baat kyun hai.',
  'A summariser with a survival test':
    'Ek summariser, survival test ke saath',
  'Build a summariser for a real document type and the specific test that proves it keeps what matters. The test is the deliverable — the prompt is easy and everybody has one.':
    'Kisi asli document type ke liye summariser banaiye aur woh khaas test jo saabit kare ki woh zaroori cheezein rakhta hai. Deliverable test hai — prompt aasaan hai aur woh sabke paas hai.',
  'Name the reader and the decision. If you cannot name a decision, the summary has no purpose and no test.':
    'Padhne waale aur faisle ka naam lijiye. Agar aap kisi faisle ka naam nahi le sakte, to summary ka na koi maksad hai na koi test.',
  'Take ten real documents and write down, for each, the two or three facts a reader would be angry to lose.':
    'Das asli documents lijiye aur har ek ke liye woh do-teen facts likhiye jinke khone par padhne waala naaraz ho jaayega.',
  'Build the summariser and run the survival check across all ten. Record the miss rate.':
    'Summariser banaiye aur dason par survival check chalaiye. Miss rate note kijiye.',
  'Make one change — an instruction about what must be preserved verbatim — and re-measure.':
    'Ek badlaav kijiye — ek instruction ki kya hoobahoo bacha rehna chahiye — aur dobara naapiye.',
  'Find a document where a fact survived in different wording and your check missed it. Note what that means about your number.':
    'Aisa document dhoondhiye jisme koi fact alag shabdon me bach gaya ho aur aapka check use pakad na paaya ho. Note kijiye ki iska aapke number ke baare me kya matlab hai.',
  'Write the note to whoever asked for this feature: what it keeps, what it drops, and the miss rate you measured.':
    'Jisne yeh feature maanga tha use note likhiye: yeh kya rakhta hai, kya chhodta hai, aur aapne kaunsi miss rate naapi.',
  'You have a miss rate from ten documents, before and after one change.':
    'Aapke paas das documents se ek miss rate hai, ek badlaav se pehle aur baad ki.',
  'You found at least one case your own test scores unfairly, and you say so.':
    'Aapko kam se kam ek aisa case mila jise aapka apna test galat score deta hai, aur aap yeh keh dete hain.',
  'The note names what the summary is for, so somebody else could test it the same way next quarter.':
    'Note me likha hai ki summary kis kaam ke liye hai, taaki koi doosra agle quarter usi tarah jaanch sake.',
  'Some shapes have no right answer':
    'Kuchh shapes ka sahi jawaab hota hi nahi',
  'Summarising is the first one you meet.':
    'Summarise karna pehli aisi shape hai jo aapko milti hai.',
  'Per-class counting beats an overall number':
    'Har class ki ginti kul number se behtar hai',
  'The same instinct, applied where counting is harder.':
    'Wahi soch, wahan lagaayi gayi jahan ginna mushkil hai.',
  'You will summarise the same document several ways.':
    'Aap ek hi document ko kai tareeke se summarise karenge.',
  'Open <code>chapter-2-5</code> and bring one real document with something consequential buried in it — a deadline, an exception, a liability, a number somebody would be angry to miss.':
    '<code>chapter-2-5</code> kholiye aur ek asli document laaiye jisme koi zaroori cheez dabi ho — koi deadline, koi apwaad, koi zimmedari, koi number jiske chhootne par koi naaraz hoga.',
  'Watch a good summary fail':
    'Ek achchhi summary ko fail hote dekhiye',
  'Summarise your document with the plainest possible instruction, then go looking for the buried thing.':
    'Apne document ko sabse saade instruction se summarise kijiye, phir dabi hui cheez dhoondhne jaaiye.',
  'A well-organised, fluent, entirely reasonable summary — which very often does not contain the buried line. It is not wrong. Nothing in it is false. It simply made an even compression of a document whose value was not evenly distributed.':
    'Ek achchhi tarah sajaayi hui, bahti hui, poori tarah waajib summary — jisme aksar woh dabi hui line hoti hi nahi. Woh galat nahi hai. Usme kuchh bhi jhooth nahi hai. Usne bas us document ko baraabar daba diya jiski keemat baraabar bati hui thi hi nahi.',
  'That is the failure mode, and it is invisible. A summary that lost the one line that mattered looks exactly like a summary that kept it.':
    'Yahi failure hai, aur yeh dikhti nahi. Jis summary se ek zaroori line chhoot gayi woh bilkul us summary jaisi dikhti hai jisne use rakh liya.',
  'Which is why the first question is never "how do I summarise this?" It is "who reads this, and what will they do next?" A summary has no quality on its own. It only has fitness for a decision.':
    'Isiliye pehla sawaal kabhi “ise summarise kaise karun?” nahi hota. Woh hota hai “ise padhta kaun hai, aur uske baad woh karega kya?” Summary ki apne aap me koi quality nahi hoti. Uski sirf kisi faisle ke liye upyogita hoti hai.',
  'Same document, three readers':
    'Wahi document, teen padhne waale',
  'Summarise it three times, naming a different reader and decision each time.':
    'Use teen baar summarise kijiye, har baar alag padhne waala aur alag faisla naam lete hue.',
  'Three genuinely different documents. The lawyer version keeps the obligations and drops the story; the new joiner version does the reverse. Neither is better. They are answers to different questions, and the plain version was silently an answer to none of them.':
    'Teen sach me alag documents. Vakeel waala version zimmedariyaan rakhta hai aur kahani chhod deta hai; naye saathi waala ulta karta hai. Koi behtar nahi hai. Woh alag sawaalon ke jawaab hain, aur saada version chupchaap kisi ka bhi jawaab nahi tha.',
  'So a summariser can be tested after all — not by grading the prose, but by asking whether specific things survived.':
    'To summariser ko jaancha ja sakta hai — prose ko number de kar nahi, balki yeh poochh kar ki khaas cheezein bachin ya nahi.',
  'You cannot grade a summary. You can absolutely test whether it kept the five things a reader would be angry to lose.':
    'Aap summary ko score nahi de sakte. Aap poori tarah jaanch sakte hain ki usne woh paanch cheezein rakhin ya nahi jinke khone par padhne waala naaraz hoga.',
  'Build the survival test':
    'Survival test banaiye',
  'For five real documents, write down the two or three facts a reader must not lose. Then check each summary for them mechanically.':
    'Paanch asli documents ke liye woh do-teen facts likhiye jo padhne waale se chhootne nahi chahiye. Phir har summary me unhe machine se jaanchiye.',
  'A concrete miss rate, on the only thing that matters. Crude — a summary can carry a fact in different words and this will not see it — and still far more useful than reading five summaries and feeling good about them.':
    'Ek thos miss rate, sirf usi cheez par jo maayne rakhti hai. Motay taur par — summary koi fact alag shabdon me le ja sakti hai aur yeh use nahi dekhega — aur phir bhi paanch summaries padh kar achchha mehsoos karne se kahin zyada kaam ka.',
  'Now change one thing. Add <em>"keep every date, amount and named party exactly as written"</em> and re-run.':
    'Ab ek cheez badliye. <em>“har date, amount aur naam hoobahoo waise hi rakhiye jaise likha hai”</em> jodiye aur dobara chalaiye.',
  'The miss rate usually drops sharply, and the summaries get slightly longer and slightly duller. That is the trade, it is yours to make, and you now have both numbers.':
    'Miss rate aam taur par tezi se girti hai, aur summaries thodi lambi aur thodi feeki ho jaati hain. Yahi sauda hai, karna aapko hai, aur ab aapke paas dono numbers hain.',
  'Two chapters, two shapes, one method: decide what would count as failure, then measure that specific thing rather than reading output and forming an impression.':
    'Do chapters, do shapes, ek tareeka: pehle tay kijiye ki failure kya kehlayegi, phir usi khaas cheez ko naapiye — output padh kar ek ehsaas banane ke bajaay.',
  'And a wall. Everything in this arc works on a document you can paste into the request. The moment the answer lives somewhere across a hundred documents — a handbook, a policy library, five years of contracts — none of it applies, because the model has never seen any of them.':
    'Aur ek deewar. Is arc ki har cheez us document par chalti hai jise aap request me paste kar sakte hain. Jis pal jawaab sau documents me kahin baitha ho — koi handbook, policy library, paanch saal ke contracts — inme se kuchh bhi kaam nahi aata, kyunki model ne unme se koi dekha hi nahi hai.',
  'Latency, and what the user does while waiting':
    'Latency, aur intezaar me user kya karta hai',
  'Why the same number of seconds can feel fast or broken, and what you put on the screen in between.':
    'Kyun utne hi second kabhi tez aur kabhi toota hua lagte hain, aur beech me screen par aap kya rakhte hain.',
  'Say why streaming changes felt speed without changing actual speed.':
    'Yeh batana ki streaming asli raftaar badle bina mehsoos hone waali raftaar kaise badal deti hai.',
  'Choose what to show during a wait, for a specific feature, and say what it costs to be wrong.':
    'Kisi khaas feature ke liye tay karna ki intezaar me kya dikhana hai, aur galat hone par uska kya kharch hai.',
  'Name the wait your own product cannot make shorter, and what you would do instead.':
    'Apne product ka woh intezaar batana jise aap chhota nahi kar sakte, aur uske badle aap kya karenge.',
  'The wait, designed':
    'Intezaar, dhang se banaya gaya',
  'Take the slowest thing you would ship and design its wait properly — with a measured number at the front, not a spinner and a hope.':
    'Jo sabse dheemi cheez aap ship karenge use lijiye aur uska intezaar dhang se design kijiye — shuru me ek naapa hua number ke saath, spinner aur ummeed ke saath nahi.',
  'Measure the real distribution, not one run: time twenty realistic requests and write down the median and the worst.':
    'Asli spread naapiye, ek run nahi: bees asli requests ka samay lijiye aur median aur sabse kharaab dono likhiye.',
  'Split the total into its parts — retrieval, thinking, generation — and mark which parts you could actually shorten.':
    'Kul samay ko hisson me baantiye — retrieval, sochna, generation — aur nishaan lagaiye ki kaunse hisse aap sach me chhote kar sakte hain.',
  'Decide whether the answer is useful in pieces. That decides streaming versus background, and write down why.':
    'Tay kijiye ki jawaab tukdon me kaam ka hai ya nahi. Wahi streaming aur background me se chunta hai, aur wajah likh lijiye.',
  'Design what is on the screen at second one, second three, and second ten. Actual words, not a placeholder.':
    'Design kijiye ki pehle second, teesre second aur dasve second par screen par kya hai. Asli shabd, koi placeholder nahi.',
  'Decide what happens at your worst case, and what the user can do about it.':
    'Tay kijiye ki sabse kharaab haalat me kya hota hai, aur user uske baare me kya kar sakta hai.',
  'Write the acceptance line: at what measured time does this feature stop being interactive and have to move to the background?':
    'Acceptance line likhiye: kis naape hue samay par yeh feature interactive rehna band kar deta hai aur use background me jaana padta hai?',
  'Your numbers are a median and a worst case from twenty runs, not an average of three.':
    'Aapke numbers bees runs ka median aur sabse kharaab haalat hain, teen ka ausat nahi.',
  'The screen has real words on it at three different moments.':
    'Screen par teen alag pal par asli shabd likhe hain.',
  'You can say the threshold at which you would change the whole interaction, and it is a number.':
    'Aap woh threshold bata sakte hain jis par aap poora interaction hi badal denge, aur woh ek number hai.',
  'Thinking is a purchase':
    'Sochna ek kharid hai',
  'You measured what it costs in money and in seconds.':
    'Aapne naapa ki uska paise aur second dono me kya kharch hai.',
  'A schema fixes the shape of a reply':
    'Schema jawaab ki shape tay kar deta hai',
  'Which is what makes a partial reply safe to show.':
    'Aur isiliye aadha jawaab dikhana surakshit ho paata hai.',
  'Open <code>chapter-11-5</code> and use whichever feature you costed in Chapter 11. You will time the same call twice and change nothing about how fast it is.':
    '<code>chapter-11-5</code> kholiye aur wahi feature lijiye jiska kharch aapne Chapter 11 me nikaala tha. Aap ek hi call ka samay do baar naapenge aur uski raftaar me kuchh nahi badlenge.',
  'Time it, then feel it':
    'Samay naapiye, phir use mehsoos kijiye',
  'Run one realistic request and time it end to end. Then run the same request streamed, and time when the <em>first</em> characters arrive.':
    'Ek asli request chalaiye aur shuru se ant tak samay lijiye. Phir wahi request stream karke chalaiye, aur naapiye ki <em>pehle</em> akshar kab aate hain.',
  'The total is the same or very slightly worse. The first words arrive in a fraction of it. Nothing got faster and the experience is completely different, because waiting with evidence that something is happening is a different act from waiting at a blank screen.':
    'Kul samay wahi rehta hai ya zara sa zyada. Pehle shabd uske ek chhote hisse me aa jaate hain. Kuchh bhi tez nahi hua aur anubhav poori tarah alag hai, kyunki yeh sabooot ke saath intezaar karna ki kuchh ho raha hai, khaali screen ke saamne intezaar karne se alag cheez hai.',
  'Your provider or model does not stream':
    'Aapka provider ya model stream nahi karta',
  'Some endpoints and some reasoning modes return only the finished answer. That is itself the finding: it means this feature cannot use the cheapest trick available for felt speed, and the rest of the chapter is what you do instead.':
    'Kuchh endpoints aur kuchh reasoning modes sirf poora jawaab lautate hain. Yeh khud ek khoj hai: matlab yeh feature mehsoos hone waali raftaar ka sabse sasta tareeka istemaal nahi kar sakta, aur baaki chapter wahi hai jo aap uske badle karte hain.',
  'Perceived speed is about when something starts, not when it finishes. Almost every wait you can improve, you improve at the front.':
    'Mehsoos hone waali raftaar is baat par hai ki cheez shuru kab hoti hai, khatm kab hoti hai us par nahi. Lagbhag har woh intezaar jise aap behtar kar sakte hain, aap shuruaat me behtar karte hain.',
  'Which gives you three honest options for any wait, and they are not equally good.':
    'Jisse kisi bhi intezaar ke liye teen imaandaar vikalp milte hain, aur woh baraabar achchhe nahi hain.',
  '<strong>Start early.</strong> Stream, or show the first step of a multi-step job as it completes. Costs nothing and helps most.':
    '<strong>Jaldi shuru kijiye.</strong> Stream kijiye, ya kai steps waale kaam ka pehla step poora hote hi dikha dijiye. Kuchh kharch nahi hota aur sabse zyada madad karta hai.',
  '<strong>Say what is happening.</strong> Not a spinner — the actual step. “Reading 6 documents” tells a person the wait is proportionate to the job.':
    '<strong>Bataiye ki ho kya raha hai.</strong> Spinner nahi — asli step. “6 documents padh raha hai” insaan ko batata hai ki intezaar kaam ke hisaab se hai.',
  '<strong>Take the wait somewhere else.</strong> If it is genuinely long, stop pretending it is interactive. Do it in the background and tell them when it is done.':
    '<strong>Intezaar ko kahin aur le jaaiye.</strong> Agar woh sach me lamba hai, to yeh dikhawa band kijiye ki woh interactive hai. Use background me kijiye aur poora hone par bata dijiye.',
  'The third is the one teams avoid, because it feels like an admission. It is usually the right answer for anything over about ten seconds, and it removes the problem rather than dressing it.':
    'Teesre se teams bachti hain, kyunki woh haar maanne jaisa lagta hai. Lagbhag das second se upar ki har cheez ke liye aam taur par wahi sahi jawaab hai, aur woh samasya ko sajaane ke bajaay hata deta hai.',
  'Watch a spinner lie':
    'Spinner ko jhooth bolte dekhiye',
  'Take the slowest realistic request you have and run it while looking at a clock. Now imagine two screens: one with a spinner, one with the words <em>reading 6 documents · comparing against policy</em> and a step counter.':
    'Apni sabse dheemi asli request lijiye aur ghadi dekhte hue chalaiye. Ab do screens sochiye: ek me spinner, doosri me likha <em>6 documents padh raha hai · policy se mila raha hai</em> aur ek step counter.',
  'The same seconds. In the first, the user cannot tell a slow answer from a broken one, so their honest move at eight seconds is to reload — which costs you the whole call and starts it again. In the second, they can see it is working and roughly how far along.':
    'Utne hi second. Pehli me user dheeme jawaab aur toote hue jawaab me farq nahi kar sakta, isliye aathve second par uska imaandaar kadam reload karna hai — jo aapko poori call ka kharch deta hai aur use dobara shuru karta hai. Doosri me use dikhta hai ki kaam ho raha hai aur motay taur par kahan tak.',
  'An undifferentiated spinner is not a neutral choice. It teaches people to reload, and every reload is a call you paid for twice.':
    'Bina kuchh bataye spinner koi tatasth chunaav nahi hai. Woh logon ko reload karna sikhata hai, aur har reload ek aisi call hai jiska daam aapne do baar chukaya.',
  'What you would change':
    'Aap kya badlenge',
  'Your feature takes nine seconds and cannot be made faster. You can stream the answer, or move it to the background and notify. Which, and on what does it depend?':
    'Aapka feature nau second leta hai aur ise tez nahi kiya ja sakta. Aap jawaab stream kar sakte hain, ya use background me le ja kar baad me bata sakte hain. Kaunsa, aur yeh kis par tika hai?',
  'On whether the answer is useful in pieces. If reading the first sentence starts the person’s work — a draft, an explanation, a summary — stream it. If it is only useful complete — a decision, a routed ticket, a filled form — streaming shows them a half-answer they must not act on, and the background is safer.':
    'Is par ki jawaab tukdon me kaam ka hai ya nahi. Agar pehla vaakya padhte hi insaan ka kaam shuru ho jaata hai — koi draft, vyakhya, summary — to stream kijiye. Agar woh sirf poora hone par kaam ka hai — koi faisla, bheja gaya ticket, bhara hua form — to streaming use aadha jawaab dikhati hai jispar use amal nahi karna chahiye, aur background zyada surakshit hai.',
  'This is why the chapter needed the schema chapter behind it. A partial reply is safe to show precisely when its shape means the visible part is already true. A half-streamed <em>decision</em> field is not a decision, it is a hazard.':
    'Isiliye is chapter ko schema waala chapter peechhe chahiye tha. Aadha jawaab dikhana theek tab surakshit hai jab uski shape ka matlab ho ki jo hissa dikh raha hai woh pehle se sach hai. Aadha stream hua <em>decision</em> field koi faisla nahi, ek khatra hai.',
  'None of this made anything faster. All of it changed whether nine seconds is acceptable, which is the only version of the question your users are actually asking.':
    'Isme se kisi ne kuchh tez nahi kiya. In sab ne yeh badla ki nau second sweekaar hain ya nahi, aur aapke users asal me yahi sawaal poochh rahe hain.',
  'What you may send':
    'Aap kya bhej sakte hain',
  'The question nobody puts in a design doc and everybody asks at their desk: am I allowed to paste this in?':
    'Woh sawaal jo koi design doc me nahi likhta aur har koi apni desk par poochhta hai: kya main ise paste kar sakta hoon?',
  'Decide, for a specific document, whether it may be sent — and say what the decision rests on.':
    'Kisi khaas document ke liye tay karna ki use bheja ja sakta hai ya nahi — aur batana ki yeh faisla kis par tika hai.',
  'Name the three questions that settle it, in the order that resolves most cases fastest.':
    'Un teen sawaalon ka naam lena jo ise tay karte hain, us kram me jo zyadatar cases sabse jaldi nipta de.',
  'Design a way for colleagues to get this right without asking you.':
    'Aisa tareeka banana jisse saathi bina aapse poochhe yeh sahi kar sakein.',
  'The rule, and the file behind it':
    'Niyam, aur uske peechhe ki file',
  'Produce the one-page answer to "may I send this?" for your own team, backed by what the vendor actually says rather than what everyone assumes.':
    'Apni team ke liye “kya main ise bhej sakta hoon?” ka ek page ka jawaab banaiye, jo us par tika ho jo vendor sach me kehta hai, us par nahi jo sab maan lete hain.',
  'List the document types your team would realistically want to send. Six to ten.':
    'Un document types ki list banaiye jinhe aapki team sach me bhejna chahegi. Chhah se das.',
  'Run each through the three questions and mark it may-send, never-send, or ask.':
    'Har ek ko teen sawaalon se guzariye aur use bhej-sakte-hain, kabhi-nahi, ya poochhna hai ka nishaan dijiye.',
  'For the ask column, name who is asked and how long they take. If that answer is unpleasant, the column is too big.':
    'Poochhna hai waale column ke liye bataiye ki kis se poochha jaata hai aur unhe kitna samay lagta hai. Agar woh jawaab bura lage, to column bahut bada hai.',
  'Find and write down, with dates, what your main vendor says about retention, training and location — for the plan you are actually on.':
    'Dhoondh kar, taareekh ke saath likhiye ki aapka mukhya vendor retention, training aur location ke baare me kya kehta hai — us plan ke liye jispar aap sach me hain.',
  'Check the retrieval case: what is in your corpus, and would every item in it pass your own rule?':
    'Retrieval waala maamla jaanchiye: aapke corpus me kya hai, aur kya usme har cheez aapke apne niyam par khari utregi?',
  'Write the one page, and give it to a colleague to use on a document you have not seen.':
    'Ek page likhiye, aur use kisi saathi ko dijiye ki woh use aise document par istemaal kare jo aapne dekha hi nahi.',
  'A colleague used it on a real document without asking you a question.':
    'Kisi saathi ne use asli document par istemaal kiya, bina aapse ek bhi sawaal poochhe.',
  'The vendor answers are quoted with a date and a plan name, not remembered.':
    'Vendor ke jawaab taareekh aur plan ke naam ke saath likhe hain, yaad kiye hue nahi.',
  'You checked the corpus against your own rule and either it passes or you know what has to come out.':
    'Aapne corpus ko apne hi niyam ke against jaancha aur ya to woh khara utarta hai, ya aap jaante hain ki usme se kya hataana hai.',
  'Everything you send leaves your building':
    'Jo bhi aap bhejte hain woh aapki imaarat se bahar jaata hai',
  'And you pay for it by the piece.':
    'Aur uska daam aap tukdon ke hisaab se chukate hain.',
  'A corpus is not what you think it is':
    'Corpus woh nahi hai jo aap samajhte hain',
  'You audited what your documents actually contain.':
    'Aapne audit kiya tha ki aapke documents me asal me hai kya.',
  'No code. Bring three real documents from your work: one you are certain is fine to send, one you are certain is not, and one you genuinely do not know about. The third is the useful one.':
    'Koi code nahi. Apne kaam ke teen asli documents laaiye: ek jise bhejna aapko pakka theek lagta hai, ek jise pakka nahi, aur ek jiske baare me aap sach me nahi jaante. Teesra hi kaam ka hai.',
  'Every chapter so far has assumed you may send the text. For most of what you will build, that assumption is either fine or catastrophic, and the difference is not technical.':
    'Ab tak har chapter ne yeh maan liya tha ki aap text bhej sakte hain. Aap jo banayenge uske zyadatar hisse ke liye yeh maanyata ya to theek hai ya bhayankar, aur farq technical nahi hai.',
  'This is not a legal chapter and you are not being asked to become a lawyer. It is a chapter about knowing which three questions to ask, and who owns the answer to each.':
    'Yeh koi kanooni chapter nahi hai aur aapse vakeel banne ko nahi kaha ja raha. Yeh chapter is baare me hai ki kaunse teen sawaal poochhne hain, aur har ek ka jawaab kiske paas hai.',
  'Sort your three, and notice where the difficulty is':
    'Apne teenon ko chhaantiye, aur dekhiye ki mushkil kahan hai',
  'For each of the three documents, answer in one line each: does it contain information about an identifiable person; is it commercially confidential; and did somebody outside your organisation give it to you under terms?':
    'Teenon documents ke liye ek-ek line me jawaab dijiye: kya isme kisi pehchaane ja sakne waale insaan ki jaankaari hai; kya yeh vyavsayik roop se gopniya hai; aur kya ise aapke sangathan ke bahar se kisi ne kisi shart par diya tha?',
  'The two easy documents resolve on the first question. The uncertain one almost always turns on the third — something a customer or supplier sent you, where the terms you agreed to are somewhere nobody has read recently.':
    'Dono aasaan documents pehle hi sawaal par nipat jaate hain. Anishchit waala lagbhag hamesha teesre par atakta hai — koi cheez jo kisi customer ya supplier ne bheji thi, jahan aapne jo shartein maani thin woh kahin padi hain aur haal me kisi ne padhi nahi.',
  'The hard cases are rarely about personal data. They are about obligations somebody else’s contract put on you.':
    'Mushkil maamle virle hi niji data ke hote hain. Woh un zimmedariyon ke hote hain jo kisi aur ke contract ne aap par daal di thin.',
  'Three questions, in the order that settles most cases with least effort.':
    'Teen sawaal, us kram me jo sabse kam mehnat me zyadatar maamle nipta de.',
  '<strong>Is there a person in it?</strong> Names, contact details, case references, anything that identifies somebody. This has rules attached wherever you are, and they are not optional.':
    '<strong>Kya isme koi insaan hai?</strong> Naam, contact, case reference, kuchh bhi jo kisi ko pehchaane. Aap jahan bhi hon, iske saath niyam jude hain, aur woh vaikalpik nahi hain.',
  '<strong>Whose secret is it?</strong> Yours is a business decision. Somebody else’s is a contractual one, and the answer may be no regardless of how careful the vendor is.':
    '<strong>Yeh raaz kiska hai?</strong> Aapka apna ek business faisla hai. Kisi aur ka ek contract ka maamla hai, aur jawaab na ho sakta hai chaahe vendor kitna hi savdhaan ho.',
  '<strong>What does the vendor do with it?</strong> Retention, whether it trains on it, which country it sits in. All three are usually answerable from the terms in ten minutes, and all three change with the plan you are on.':
    '<strong>Vendor uska karta kya hai?</strong> Kitne din rakhta hai, us par model train karta hai ya nahi, kis desh me rakhta hai. Teenon aam taur par shartein padh kar das minute me mil jaate hain, aur teenon aapke plan ke saath badal jaate hain.',
  'The third question is where product managers add the most value, because it is the one engineers assume is settled and vendors describe in language designed to sound settled.':
    'Teesra sawaal wahi hai jahan product managers sabse zyada keemat jodte hain, kyunki engineers maan lete hain ki woh tay hai aur vendors use aisi bhasha me batate hain jo tay lagne ke liye hi banayi gayi hai.',
  'Read the actual terms for one tool you already use':
    'Jo tool aap pehle se istemaal karte hain uski asli shartein padhiye',
  'Pick a tool your team already sends text to. Find, in its own documentation, the answers to: how long is it kept, is it used to improve the model, and which country is it processed in.':
    'Koi aisa tool chuniye jise aapki team pehle se text bhejti hai. Uske apne documentation me jawaab dhoondhiye: use kitne din rakha jaata hai, kya use model behtar karne me lagaya jaata hai, aur woh kis desh me process hota hai.',
  'Two of the three are usually easy to find and one takes real digging. Note the plan those answers apply to — the free and paid tiers frequently differ on exactly the question that matters, and people sign up on the free one.':
    'Teen me se do aam taur par aasaani se mil jaate hain aur ek me sach me khodna padta hai. Note kijiye ki woh jawaab kis plan par laagu hote hain — free aur paid tiers aksar theek us sawaal par alag hote hain jo maayne rakhta hai, aur log free waale par sign up karte hain.',
  'Write the three answers down with the date. This is the beginning of the vendor file Chapter 17 asks for, and now it exists because you needed it rather than because a form demanded it.':
    'Teenon jawaab taareekh ke saath likh lijiye. Yahi woh vendor file ki shuruaat hai jo Chapter 17 maangta hai, aur ab woh isliye maujood hai kyunki aapko zaroorat thi, isliye nahi ki kisi form ne maangi.',
  'Write the rule a colleague could follow without asking you. Not a policy — three or four lines that resolve the common cases and say clearly what to do with the rest.':
    'Woh niyam likhiye jise koi saathi bina aapse poochhe follow kar sake. Policy nahi — teen-chaar line jo aam maamle nipta dein aur saaf batayein ki baaki ka kya karna hai.',
  'You may send … . Never send … . If it came from a customer, … . If unsure, … .':
    'Aap bhej sakte hain … . Kabhi mat bhejiye … . Agar woh customer se aaya hai, … . Agar shak ho, … .',
  'The rules that work share a shape: they resolve the frequent cases outright, they name one clear category that is never sent, and they give an explicit route for the uncertain ones that does not depend on someone’s judgement in the moment. The rules that fail are the ones that say "use discretion" — because a person who is unsure and in a hurry will read that as permission. The escape hatch has to be a person or a channel, named.':
    'Jo niyam chalte hain unki ek shape hoti hai: woh aam maamle wahin nipta dete hain, ek saaf category ka naam lete hain jo kabhi nahi bheji jaati, aur anishchit waalon ke liye ek saaf raasta dete hain jo us pal kisi ki raay par tika na ho. Jo niyam fail hote hain woh “apne vivek se kaam lijiye” kehte hain — kyunki jo insaan anishchit hai aur jaldi me hai woh use ijaazat padhega. Nikaas ka raasta koi insaan ya koi channel hona chahiye, naam ke saath.',
  'One more thing, and it is the one that catches careful teams. Retrieval sends whatever it retrieves. You may have decided carefully what goes into the corpus and then built a system that pulls three chunks at random from it into every request. The decision you made about the corpus is the decision you made about every query.':
    'Ek aur baat, aur yahi savdhaan teams ko pakadti hai. Retrieval jo bhi laata hai woh bhej deta hai. Ho sakta hai aapne bahut soch kar tay kiya ho ki corpus me kya jaayega, aur phir aisa system bana diya ho jo usme se teen chunks har request me utha laata hai. Corpus ke baare me aapne jo faisla liya, wahi faisla aapne har query ke baare me liya.',
  'Build or buy':
    'Banayein ya khareedein',
  'The commonest real decision, and the small number of things that actually settle it.':
    'Sabse aam asli faisla, aur woh chand cheezein jo use sach me tay karti hain.',
  'Run the same evaluation against a vendor and against your own build, and compare like with like.':
    'Ek hi evaluation ko vendor par aur apne apne build par chalana, aur ek jaisi cheezon ki tulna karna.',
  'Name what you are really buying, which is usually not the model.':
    'Yeh batana ki aap asal me khareed kya rahe hain, jo aam taur par model nahi hota.',
  'Say what would make you change the decision later, before you make it.':
    'Faisla lene se pehle yeh batana ki aage chal kar kaunsi cheez use badal degi.',
  'The recommendation, with its own expiry date':
    'Sifaarish, apni expiry date ke saath',
  'Make a real build-or-buy recommendation on evidence you generated, including the conditions under which it stops being right.':
    'Apne banaye sabooot par ek asli banayein-ya-khareedein sifaarish kijiye, un shaton samet jinke aane par woh sahi rehna band kar deti hai.',
  'State the capability in one line, and whether it is core or supporting to what your product is for.':
    'Kaabiliyat ko ek line me likhiye, aur yeh ki woh aapke product ke maksad ke liye mool hai ya sahayak.',
  'Run your answer key against at least one vendor trial and record the numbers beside your own build’s.':
    'Apni answer key ko kam se kam ek vendor trial par chalaiye aur numbers apne build ke numbers ke saath likhiye.',
  'Cost both over two years, including evaluation, maintenance and the on-call.':
    'Dono ka do saal ka kharch nikaaliye, jisme evaluation, maintenance aur on-call shaamil ho.',
  'Add time-to-user for both. Say which matters more here and why.':
    'Dono ke liye user tak pahunchne ka samay jodiye. Bataiye ki yahan kaunsa zyada maayne rakhta hai aur kyun.',
  'Write the exit answer for the buy option: what you would need to leave, and how long it would take.':
    'Khareedne waale vikalp ke liye nikaas ka jawaab likhiye: nikalne ke liye aapko kya chahiye hoga, aur usme kitna samay lagega.',
  'Write the two triggers that would reverse the decision, and the date you will re-read them.':
    'Woh do trigger likhiye jo faisla palat denge, aur woh taareekh jab aap unhe dobara padhenge.',
  'Both options were measured against the same answer key, by you.':
    'Dono vikalp ek hi answer key ke against naape gaye, aapke dwara.',
  'The build cost includes the maintenance and evaluation, not just the tokens.':
    'Build ke kharch me maintenance aur evaluation shaamil hain, sirf tokens nahi.',
  'The recommendation names what would make it wrong, with a date attached.':
    'Sifaarish batati hai ki kaunsi cheez use galat kar degi, aur uske saath ek taareekh hai.',
  'A spec is a measured range':
    'Spec ek naapi hui range hai',
  'So you can state what "good enough" means before shopping.':
    'Isliye aap khareedne se pehle bata sakte hain ki “kaafi achchha” ka matlab kya hai.',
  'You can measure retrieval yourself':
    'Retrieval aap khud naap sakte hain',
  'Which is what lets you test a vendor rather than believe one.':
    'Aur isiliye aap vendor par bharosa karne ke bajaay use jaanch sakte hain.',
  'No new setup. Bring the acceptance criteria from Chapter 18 and the answer key from Chapter 6. Those two artefacts are what turn this from an opinion into a comparison.':
    'Koi naya setup nahi. Chapter 18 ke acceptance criteria aur Chapter 6 ki answer key le aaiye. Yeh do cheezein hi ise raay se tulna me badal deti hain.',
  'Somebody will propose buying a product that does what you have spent this course learning to build. The conversation usually turns on price and demo quality, and both are close to irrelevant.':
    'Koi na koi aisa product khareedne ka prastav rakhega jo wahi karta hai jo aap is course me banana seekh rahe hain. Baatcheet aam taur par daam aur demo ki quality par ghoomti hai, aur dono lagbhag bemtlab hain.',
  'You are almost never buying the model. Everybody has the same models. You are buying the connectors, the permissions, the audit trail, the support contract, and somebody else carrying the on-call.':
    'Aap lagbhag kabhi model nahi khareed rahe hote. Models sabke paas wahi hain. Aap khareed rahe hain connectors, permissions, audit trail, support contract, aur yeh ki on-call koi aur uthaye.',
  'Run your own answer key against the vendor':
    'Apni answer key vendor par chalaiye',
  'Ask for a trial, put your ten real questions through it, and grade them against the key you already have. Not their demo questions. Yours.':
    'Trial maangiye, apne das asli sawaal usme daaliye, aur unhe usi key ke against jaanchiye jo aapke paas pehle se hai. Unke demo sawaal nahi. Aapke.',
  'Almost always worse than the demo suggested and better than you feared. And the two rows that matter — the unanswerable question and the one in another language — are usually where the gap is widest, because those are the rows nobody optimises for.':
    'Lagbhag hamesha demo se kharaab aur aapke dar se behtar. Aur jo do rows maayne rakhti hain — bina jawaab waala sawaal aur doosri bhasha waala — wahin farq sabse bada hota hai, kyunki un rows ke liye koi optimise nahi karta.',
  'You are the only person in this negotiation who can run this test, because you are the only one with the answer key.':
    'Is baatcheet me yeh test sirf aap chala sakte hain, kyunki answer key sirf aapke paas hai.',
  'Then the part that decides it, which has nothing to do with quality.':
    'Phir woh hissa jo faisla karta hai, aur jiska quality se koi lena-dena nahi.',
  'question':
    'sawaal',
  'why it settles things':
    'yeh cheezein kyun tay kar deta hai',
  'Is this a core capability or a supporting one?':
    'Kya yeh mool kaabiliyat hai ya sahayak?',
  'If your product’s reason to exist is this, owning it is not optional. If it is plumbing, buying is almost always right.':
    'Agar aapke product ke hone ki wajah yahi hai, to ise apna rakhna vaikalpik nahi hai. Agar yeh plumbing hai, to khareedna lagbhag hamesha sahi hai.',
  'How fast does it need to change?':
    'Ise kitni tezi se badalna hoga?',
  'Something you will tune weekly against your own data is painful to buy. Something stable is painful to build.':
    'Jise aap apne data par har hafte tune karenge use khareedna takleef deta hai. Jo sthir hai use banana takleef deta hai.',
  'Who is on call at 2am?':
    'Raat do baje on-call kaun hai?',
  'A real cost, usually left out, and often larger than the licence.':
    'Ek asli kharch, aam taur par chhoda hua, aur aksar licence se bada.',
  'What happens if they are acquired or shut down?':
    'Agar unhe koi khareed le ya woh band ho jaayein to kya hoga?',
  'Ask what you would need to leave, and how long it would take. If nobody can answer, that is the answer.':
    'Poochhiye ki nikalne ke liye aapko kya chahiye hoga, aur usme kitna samay lagega. Agar koi jawaab na de sake, to wahi jawaab hai.',
  'Cost both sides honestly':
    'Dono taraf ka kharch imaandaari se nikaaliye',
  'Write the two-year cost of each. For build, include what you learnt in Chapter 15 plus the parts nobody puts in: evaluation, the person maintaining it, and doing the migration rehearsal every time the model underneath changes.':
    'Dono ka do saal ka kharch likhiye. Build ke liye Chapter 15 me jo seekha woh jodiye, aur woh hisse bhi jo koi nahi jodta: evaluation, use sambhaalne waala insaan, aur har baar neeche ka model badalne par migration ki rehearsal.',
  'The build column is usually two to four times the number people first say, and the buy column has a growth clause somebody has not read. Neither of those surprises should arrive after the decision.':
    'Build waala column aam taur par us number ka do se chaar guna hota hai jo log pehle batate hain, aur buy waale column me ek growth clause hota hai jise kisi ne padha nahi. In dono me se koi hairaani faisle ke baad nahi aani chahiye.',
  'Then the number that is not money: how long until each option is in front of a user. A build that is cheaper over two years and six months later can still be the wrong answer.':
    'Phir woh number jo paisa nahi hai: har vikalp user ke saamne kab tak pahunchega. Jo build do saal me sasta ho aur chhah maheene baad aaye, woh phir bhi galat jawaab ho sakta hai.',
  'Write down what would make you change your mind — in both directions. What evidence would turn your build recommendation into a buy, and what would turn a buy into a build?':
    'Likhiye ki kaunsi cheez aapka mann badal degi — dono dishaon me. Kaunsa sabooot aapki build waali sifaarish ko buy me badal dega, aur kaunsa buy ko build me?',
  'I would switch to buying if … . I would switch to building if … .':
    'Main khareedne par chala jaaunga agar … . Main banane par chala jaaunga agar … .',
  'Writing this before deciding is what stops the decision from becoming an identity. The usual triggers for switching to buy are the maintenance cost landing on one person and the capability turning out to be commodity. The usual triggers the other way are the vendor’s roadmap diverging from your need, the price step at the next tier, and discovering that the thing you thought was plumbing is the thing customers actually choose you for. Put a date on when you will re-read this.':
    'Faisla lene se pehle yeh likh lena hi use pehchaan banne se rokta hai. Buy par jaane ke aam trigger yeh hain ki maintenance ka bojh ek hi insaan par aa gira, aur yeh ki kaabiliyat aam nikli. Ulti disha ke aam trigger yeh hain ki vendor ka roadmap aapki zaroorat se alag ho gaya, agle tier par daam ki chhalaang, aur yeh pata chalna ki jise aap plumbing samajh rahe the wahi cheez hai jiske liye customers aapko chunte hain. Ek taareekh daaliye ki aap ise dobara kab padhenge.',
  'And one shape worth knowing, because it is often the correct answer and rarely the one proposed: buy the plumbing, build the part that is yours. Somebody else’s connectors and permissions, your retrieval and your evaluation.':
    'Aur ek shape jaanne laayak hai, kyunki woh aksar sahi jawaab hoti hai aur virle hi prastavit hoti hai: plumbing khareed lijiye, jo hissa aapka hai woh banaiye. Kisi aur ke connectors aur permissions, aapka retrieval aur aapka evaluation.',
  'Proving it helped':
    'Yeh saabit karna ki isse madad hui',
  'System quality and business impact are different measurements, and the course has so far only taught the first.':
    'System ki quality aur business par asar do alag maap hain, aur course ne ab tak sirf pehla sikhaya hai.',
  'Design a pilot that could actually show the feature did not help.':
    'Aisa pilot design karna jo sach me dikha sake ki feature se madad nahi hui.',
  'Name the one number the business cares about, and how the feature would move it.':
    'Woh ek number batana jiski business ko parwah hai, aur yeh ki feature use kaise hilaayega.',
  'Explain why a measurably good system can produce no measurable benefit.':
    'Yeh samjhana ki naap me achchha system bhi naapne laayak koi faayda kyun nahi de paata.',
  'The pilot, designed so it could fail':
    'Pilot, is tarah banaya gaya ki woh fail ho sake',
  'Design a pilot for a real feature — with a number the business already tracks, a comparison, a floor, and a window. Then get somebody senior to agree the floor before it runs.':
    'Kisi asli feature ke liye pilot design kijiye — us number ke saath jise business pehle se track karta hai, ek tulna, ek farsh aur ek samay-seema. Phir chalne se pehle kisi senior se us farsh par sehmati lijiye.',
  'Time the whole workflow end to end and mark where your feature sits. If it is not on the critical path, say so and stop here.':
    'Poore workflow ka shuru se ant tak samay naapiye aur nishaan lagaiye ki aapka feature kahan baithta hai. Agar woh critical path par nahi hai, to yeh keh dijiye aur yahin ruk jaaiye.',
  'Choose the business number. It must be one that already exists and that somebody already looks at.':
    'Business number chuniye. Woh aisa hona chahiye jo pehle se maujood hai aur jise koi pehle se dekhta hai.',
  'Design the comparison: which two groups, over which period, and what makes them comparable.':
    'Tulna design kijiye: kaunse do samooh, kis avdhi me, aur unhe tulnaayogya kya banata hai.',
  'Write the floor — the movement below which you would call this a failure — and the window before you would judge.':
    'Farsh likhiye — woh badlaav jiske neeche aap ise failure kahenge — aur woh samay-seema jiske baad aap faisla karenge.',
  'Write the disappointing sentence in advance, in the words you would say to whoever funded it.':
    'Nirasha waala vaakya pehle hi likh lijiye, un shabdon me jo aap us insaan se kahenge jisne iske liye paisa diya.',
  'Get the person who funds it to agree the floor <em>before</em> the pilot runs, in writing.':
    'Jo iske liye paisa deta hai usse pilot chalne se <em>pehle</em>, likhit me, farsh par sehmati lijiye.',
  'The number is one the business already tracked before you arrived.':
    'Woh number aisa hai jise business aapke aane se pehle bhi track karta tha.',
  'The floor is agreed in writing by the person who would be disappointed by it.':
    'Farsh par us insaan ne likhit me sehmati di hai jise uske na hone par nirasha hogi.',
  'You can describe an outcome that would make you recommend switching the feature off.':
    'Aap aisa ek nateeja bata sakte hain jiske aane par aap feature band karne ki sifaarish karenge.',
  'You can measure the system':
    'Aap system naap sakte hain',
  'Recall, precision, judges, per-class counts.':
    'Recall, precision, judges, har class ki ginti.',
  'The interface has four states':
    'Interface ki chaar states hoti hain',
  'What the user sees decides whether quality reaches them.':
    'User ko kya dikhta hai, isse tay hota hai ki quality us tak pahunchti bhi hai ya nahi.',
  'No code. Bring a feature you have measured — yours or one from the course — and the name of whoever pays for it.':
    'Koi code nahi. Koi aisa feature laaiye jise aapne naapa hai — apna ya course ka — aur us insaan ka naam jo uske liye paisa deta hai.',
  'Everything the course has measured so far is the system: is the retrieval right, is the judge trustworthy, is the classifier accurate per class. All necessary. None of it answers the question that gets the next round of funding.':
    'Ab tak course ne jo naapa hai woh system hai: retrieval sahi hai ya nahi, judge bharosemand hai ya nahi, classifier har class par kitna sahi hai. Sab zaroori. Inme se koi bhi us sawaal ka jawaab nahi deta jisse agla funding round milta hai.',
  'A system can be 94 per cent accurate and change nothing, because nobody uses it, or because the thing it accelerates was never the slow part.':
    'Koi system 94 pratishat sahi ho sakta hai aur kuchh na badle, kyunki use koi istemaal hi nahi karta, ya kyunki jise woh tez kar raha hai woh dheema hissa tha hi nahi.',
  'Find the slow part before you speed anything up':
    'Kuchh tez karne se pehle dheema hissa dhoondhiye',
  'Take the workflow your feature sits inside and time it, honestly, end to end. Every step, including the waiting-for-someone-else steps.':
    'Jis workflow ke andar aapka feature baithta hai use lijiye aur imaandaari se, shuru se ant tak samay naapiye. Har step, un steps samet jinme kisi aur ka intezaar hota hai.',
  'The AI step is almost never the biggest number. Very often the largest block is waiting for a person, or a handover between two systems, and a feature that makes a four-minute step into a one-minute step inside a three-day process has done nothing anyone will notice.':
    'AI waala step lagbhag kabhi sabse bada number nahi hota. Bahut baar sabse bada hissa kisi insaan ka intezaar hota hai, ya do systems ke beech ka hand-over — aur jo feature teen din ki process ke andar chaar minute ke step ko ek minute ka kar deta hai, usne aisa kuchh nahi kiya jo kisi ko dikhega.',
  'This is the cheapest study in the whole course and it is the one most often skipped, because it can tell you not to build the thing.':
    'Yeh poore course ka sabse sasta adhyayan hai aur sabse zyada chhoda jaane waala, kyunki yeh aapko yeh bhi bata sakta hai ki cheez banaiye hi mat.',
  'If the step you are accelerating is genuinely on the critical path, then you can design a pilot. A pilot is not a launch with a smaller audience. It is a question with a stated answer that would disappoint you.':
    'Agar jis step ko aap tez kar rahe hain woh sach me critical path par hai, to aap pilot design kar sakte hain. Pilot chhote audience waala launch nahi hai. Woh ek sawaal hai jiska ek bataya hua jawaab aapko nirash karega.',
  '<strong>The number.</strong> One measure the business already tracks — handling time, first-contact resolution, backlog age, error rate. Not a new metric invented for this.':
    '<strong>Number.</strong> Ek aisi maap jise business pehle se track karta hai — handling time, pehli baar me hal, backlog ki umar, error rate. Iske liye banayi gayi koi nayi metric nahi.',
  '<strong>The comparison.</strong> Same team before and after is weak; two comparable groups over the same period is much stronger, and usually possible.':
    '<strong>Tulna.</strong> Ek hi team ka pehle aur baad kamzor hai; ek hi avdhi me do tulnaayogya samooh kahin mazboot hain, aur aam taur par mumkin bhi.',
  '<strong>The floor.</strong> The movement below which you would call it a failure, written down before you start.':
    '<strong>Farsh.</strong> Woh badlaav jiske neeche aap ise failure kahenge, shuru karne se pehle likha hua.',
  '<strong>The window.</strong> Long enough for novelty to wear off. The first two weeks of any tool flatter it.':
    '<strong>Samay-seema.</strong> Itni lambi ki nayepan ka asar utar jaaye. Kisi bhi tool ke pehle do hafte use behtar dikhate hain.',
  'Write the disappointing result in advance':
    'Nirash karne waala nateeja pehle hi likh lijiye',
  'Before running anything, write the sentence you would have to say if the pilot showed no effect. Actually write it, in the words you would use to the person who funded it.':
    'Kuchh chalane se pehle woh vaakya likhiye jo aapko kehna padega agar pilot me koi asar na dikhe. Sach me likhiye, un shabdon me jo aap us insaan se kahenge jisne paisa diya.',
  'Two things fall out. You discover whether you have the floor number at all — most pilots do not. And you find out whether the pilot could ever have produced that sentence, or whether it was designed so every outcome reads as success.':
    'Do cheezein nikalti hain. Aapko pata chalta hai ki aapke paas farsh waala number hai bhi ya nahi — zyadatar pilots ke paas nahi hota. Aur yeh pata chalta hai ki pilot kabhi woh vaakya paida kar bhi sakta tha, ya use aise banaya gaya tha ki har nateeja safalta hi padha jaaye.',
  'A pilot that cannot fail is not a pilot. It is a launch with a nicer name, and everyone in the room knows it.':
    'Jo pilot fail hi nahi ho sakta woh pilot nahi hai. Woh ek launch hai jise achchha naam de diya gaya, aur kamre me sabko yeh pata hota hai.',
  'Your pilot shows the system works well and the business number does not move. Write the three explanations you would investigate first, in the order you would check them.':
    'Aapka pilot dikhata hai ki system achchha chal raha hai aur business number hilta hi nahi. Woh teen vajahen likhiye jinki aap sabse pehle jaanch karenge, usi kram me jis kram me karenge.',
  '1 … 2 … 3 …':
    '1 … 2 … 3 …',
  'The order that usually pays: first, are they using it — adoption is the commonest answer and the easiest to check. Second, does the output arrive where the decision is made, or in a separate tool somebody has to remember to open. Third, was the step you accelerated actually on the critical path. Only after those three is it worth questioning the system quality, which is the one most teams check first because it is the one they know how to measure.':
    'Jo kram aam taur par kaam aata hai: pehle, kya log ise istemaal kar rahe hain — adoption sabse aam jawaab hai aur jaanchne me sabse aasaan. Doosra, kya output wahan pahunchta hai jahan faisla hota hai, ya kisi alag tool me jise kisi ko khol kar dekhna yaad rakhna padta hai. Teesra, jis step ko aapne tez kiya woh sach me critical path par tha ya nahi. In teenon ke baad hi system ki quality par sawaal uthana laayak hai, aur wahi zyadatar teams sabse pehle jaanchti hain kyunki wahi unhe naapna aata hai.',
  'That is the whole course, and the shape of it is one idea repeated at larger and larger scale: decide what would count as failure, then measure that specific thing, rather than looking at output and forming an impression. You did it to a prompt, to a retriever, to a judge, to a bill, and now to a business case.':
    'Yahi poora course hai, aur uski shape ek hi idea hai jo badte-badte paimaane par dohraya jaata hai: pehle tay kijiye ki failure kya kehlayegi, phir usi khaas cheez ko naapiye, output dekh kar ek ehsaas banane ke bajaay. Aapne yeh ek prompt par kiya, retriever par, judge par, bill par, aur ab ek business case par.',
  'Everything else here is technique. That habit is the transferable part, and it will outlast every model named in these chapters.':
    'Baaki sab yahan technique hai. Woh aadat hi woh hissa hai jo saath jaata hai, aur woh in chapters me naam liye har model se zyada chalegi.'
});
